WEBVTT

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.080
My children depend on my income.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.480
I want protection for the next 20

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:10.840
years.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.480
But if I buy life insurance, does

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.140
every policy build cash value?

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.040
term life covers a specified period. If

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.280
the insured dies while the policy is

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:25.420
in

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.060
force, it pays under the contract. Ordinary

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.740
term insurance has no cash value.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.200
Traditional whole life is designed for permanent

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.640
protection and guaranteed cash

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.580
value under its contract. Required premiums and

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.120
conditions still matter.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.860
Permanent does not mean you can ignore

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:48.200
payments.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.300
For comparable coverage, term generally has a

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.300
lower initial premium than whole life.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.380
Compare the duration, premium structure, and cash

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:58.900
value.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.160
Do not assume every life policy works

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.040
the same way.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.880
I want permanent protection and guaranteed cash

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.360
value under the policy.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.860
That sounds different from a 20-year

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:15.520
term policy.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.480
Which type matches those features?

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.360
Traditional whole life matches that description.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.360
Remember, term means a specified coverage period

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.900
with no cash value.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.740
Whole life is designed for permanent protection

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.740
and contractual cash value.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.600
Now test the distinction.
